{"Title":"An Act relative to certain tax exemptions for non-profit educational institutions","BillNumber":"S1956","DocketNumber":"SD804","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"WFT0","Name":"Walter F. Timilty","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/WFT0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T14:05:58.297"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"WFT0","Name":"Walter F. Timilty","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/WFT0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T14:05:58.2966667"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S1956/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. Timilty, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 1956) of Walter F. Timilty for legislation relative to certain tax exemptions for non-profit educational institutions.  Revenue.","DocumentText":"\tClause (e) of paragraph Third of section 5 of chapter 59 of the General Laws, as appearing in the  2020 Official Edition, is hereby amended by adding the following sentence:- Notwithstanding the foregoing, no more than ten parcels of property used as residences may be exempt from property tax. \r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J26","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J26"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}